config BR2_PACKAGE_XVC_SERVER
	bool "xvc-server"
	help
	  Xilinx Virtual Cable (XVC) server for Linux.

	  XVC is a TCP/IP protocol (default port 2542) that lets Vivado's
	  Hardware Manager / Lab tools drive JTAG on an FPGA over the
	  network exactly as if a physical JTAG cable were attached,
	  by talking to a "debug_bridge" AXI JTAG-to-BSCAN IP core in the
	  programmable logic.

	  This installs two userspace binaries built from the same
	  xvcServer.c (XAPP1251 / Zynq UltraScale+ derivative):

	    - /usr/bin/xvcServer_ioctl
	        Talks to /dev/xilinx_xvc_driver* via ioctl().
	        Requires the xvc-driver kernel module to be loaded and
	        bound to a "xlnx,xvc" device tree node.

	    - /usr/bin/xvcServer_mmap
	        Talks to /dev/uioN via mmap(), using the kernel's generic
	        UIO framework. Requires xvc-uio (or any equivalent UIO
	        binding) and a matching "generic-uio" device tree node.

	  https://github.com/Xilinx/XilinxVirtualCable
